;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-5y5.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-5 5)
  title: "The Old Birch"
  intent: "at the foot of the fall, the oldest birch in the wood, hollow, where the moths winter, and the note you followed among them"
  bed: (wind 0.1 water 0.4 hum 0.4 drone 0.8)
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "####  %#######      #####"
   "####  %####     ||| #####"
   "####  %#        ||| #####"
   "####  %         ||| #####"
   "                ||| o    "
   "                |||######"
   "                |||######"
   "#########~~~#############"
   "#########~~~#############"
   "#########################")
  things: ((harmonic at: (17 7) overtone: 3)
           (ring-stone at: (20 5) overtone: 3)
           (lantern-moth at: (17 3) count: 8 drawn: 3))
  decor: auto)
;; The foot of the frozen fall. The chimney comes down at columns 4-5
;; between the fall's glass (column 3) and the rough rock (column 6,
;; climbable back up from the floor); its top stays closed until The
;; Frozen Fall (x-5y4) is written above.
;; The Old Birch is the three-wide trunk (columns 16-18, rows 2-7), its
;; hollow in the fifth row; H3 lies at its foot among the moths' cloud.
;; The green stone (20,5) is the door to the Glass Chute: taking H3 at
;; (17,7) puts you 3.6 tiles from it, so it rings as you take the fifth.
;; Carrying only H2 it shivers off-key and stays shut, so the caves
;; cannot be entered without H3 (the one-way chute is not a trap).
;; West under the low rock is Snow Hollow (rows 5-7).
